Miriam - review is under way on all 60 boxes. One item needs your or Jo's decision before the 13:30 cutoff; I have emailed Jo direct and am copying you.

NQ70418326 (Alex Morgan, D-0187) is staged in the destruction cage and is on today's manifest for the 14:30 collection. It has:
- a booked collection 2026-10-14T10:00 with representative Claire Morgan, identity and authority verified by Service Desk;
- your desk's note that the letters and photos were never copied and these are the only ones;
- an extension request Jo logged on 2026-10-09, but its review slot is 2026-10-13T09:00 - after the destruction;
- no registered extension approval.

So the request is slotted too late to save the box. OPS-14 s3 and s4 mean I cannot extend it or pull it myself, and a pending request is not permission. I have not changed the date.

Everything else is on track: the other 11 approved extensions all have registered prior permission and I am entering them now (rework EUR 336.00 committed, contractor reserve has 64 slots free so capacity is fine), and the other four open requests (NQ70231813, NQ74259573, NQ78224736, NQ76671589) are unstaged document-bay boxes expiring 14-16 October, so they are not at risk today and correctly wait for tomorrow's sitting. I am not treating any of them as approved.

Decision needed: if permission for NQ70418326 is registered by 13:30 I enter it, the warehouse retrieves the box by 13:45, and the full batch is released on time. If it is not registered, please tell me whether you want the batch released with that box on it or held. My recommendation is that Jo registers the approval today - it resolves the box, keeps the batch on time and avoids destroying the only copies of a family's letters two days before a verified collector is due.

I will confirm before the cutoff and send the full shift summary either way. - Storage desk (depot.desk)
